  "description": "Score the 342-row ancestor repair AGAINST THE FULL BATCH. The repair flow's own hierarchy number (83.9%) is not comparable to the batch's 37.2%: run over 342 rows in isolation only 31 of the 1,774 containment pairs survive, because a repaired row's ancestor is usually outside the subset. This splices the repair over the shipped 5,012 and re-runs the same detectors, so the before/after is like-for-like. The decision metric is n_rows_flagged (580 before) and blocker count (12 before); a repair that lowers hierarchy flags while raising blockers is not an improvement.",
